<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · site</p><h1 class="enc-title">Knowth</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">c. 3200 BCE</span></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Knowth is a <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/neolithic">Neolithic</a> passage tomb complex in the Boyne valley, County Meath, Ireland, built around 3200 BCE and part of the Brú na Bóinne World Heritage Site. Its great mound covers two passage tombs and is ringed by smaller satellite tombs, and it holds the largest collection of megalithic art in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/western-europe">Western Europe</a>. In the early <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/middle-ages">Middle Ages</a> the kings of northern Brega made it a royal residence.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/knowth.jpg" alt="Knowth" width="320" height="400" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Markiemcg1 · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:County_Meath_-_Knowth_-_20210930145613.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
